$$

From experiment I, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}
& 2.0 \times 10^{-2} \mathrm{~mol} \mathrm{~L}^{-1} \mathrm{~min}^{-1}=\mathrm{k}\left(0.1 \mathrm{~mol} \mathrm{~L}^{-1}\right) \\
& \Rightarrow k=0.2 \mathrm{~min}^{-1}
