$$

From experiment II, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}
& 4.0 \times 10^{-2} \mathrm{~mol} \mathrm{~L}^{-1} \mathrm{~min}^{-1}=0.2 \mathrm{~min}^{-1}[\mathrm{~A}] \\
& \Rightarrow[\mathrm{A}]=0.2 \mathrm{~mol} \mathrm{~L}^{-1}
