From experiment IV, we get

$$
2.0 \times 10^{-2} \mathrm{~mol} \mathrm{~L}^{-1} \mathrm{~min}^{-1}=0.2 \mathrm{~min}^{-1}[\mathrm{~A}]
$$

$$
\Rightarrow[\mathrm{A}]=0.1 \mathrm{~mol} \mathrm{~L}^{-1}
$$

$$
\begin{aligned}
& \text { (i) Half life, } t_{1 / 2}=\frac{0.693}{k} \\
